    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a structured address form to the owner-create endpoint while keeping the flat `address` input backward-compatible.\n\n**OpenAPI spec** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)\n- Added optional `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` properties to `OwnerFields` (inherited by the `Owner` response via `allOf`).\n- Removed `address` from the required list, so a structured request (addressLine1 + city, no flat address) is accepted. `address` is now documented as the composed output string.\n\n**Owner model** (`model/Owner.java`)\n- Added `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` persistent fields with getters/setters.\n\n**Controller** (`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`)\n- `validateRequiredFields` now accepts an owner that supplies **either** a non-blank `addressLine1` or a flat `address` (plus city, unchanged).\n- New `applyAddress` helper: prefers the structured form \u2014 when `addressLine1` is present it normalizes both lines, stores them, and stores the composed `address`; otherwise it normalizes and stores the flat `address` and clears the structured lines.\n- New `composeAddress` helper: returns the normalized `addressLine1`, with a single space and normalized `addressLine2` appended when present.\n- Normalization (`normalizeAddress`) applies to whichever fields are supplied, and `getAddress()` (used by the household hash, postcode/locality derivations, and the response) reflects the structured address when present, falling back to the flat value.\n\n**Schemas** \u2014 added `address_line1` / `address_line2` nullable columns to all four DB schemas (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres).\n\n**Test results:** `AcceptanceTest` \u2014 2/2 pass; full suite `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nA note on scope: the spec mentions that \"the household hash, postcode validation and locality\" read the address via the structured fields. Those derivations key off `postcode` and `city`, which are top-level request fields identical in both forms, so they already use the structured values with no behavioral change needed \u2014 the structured/flat distinction only affects the composed `address` (and `addressLine1`/`addressLine2`) that `getAddress()` exposes.",
